{"title":"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Only_sine_and_cosine_sum_formulas)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Only sine and cosine sum formulas)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the smallest positive integer solution to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c730e4c6391e30460574203e706852f16d8a11d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{19x^{\\circ}}=\\dfrac{\\cos{96^{\\circ}}+\\sin{96^{\\circ}}}{\\cos{96^{\\circ}}-\\sin{96^{\\circ}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"218\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb141aeccc6d34bf209e5069df98c898d3cec52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\cos{96^{\\circ}}+\\sin{96^{\\circ}}}{\\cos{96^{\\circ}}-\\sin{96^{\\circ}}} =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"149\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d946388e5e62410ee00feb4499fb9e12f7198a56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sin{186^{\\circ}}+\\sin{96^{\\circ}}}{\\sin{186^{\\circ}}-\\sin{96^{\\circ}}} =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20b0a96635f9774d5d63c8d7d4ba4d8ddf4875cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sin{(141^{\\circ}+45^{\\circ})}+\\sin{(141^{\\circ}-45^{\\circ})}}{\\sin{(141^{\\circ}+45^{\\circ})}-\\sin{(141^{\\circ}-45^{\\circ})}} =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"289\" height=\"43\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/8/31878686a09bd47fab80e14edfbd52a695299e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2\\sin{141^{\\circ}}\\cos{45^{\\circ}}}{2\\cos{141^{\\circ}}\\sin{45^{\\circ}}} = \\tan{141^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"219\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>The period of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometry#Tangent\" title=\"Trigonometry\">tangent</a> function is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />, and the tangent function is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=One-to-one\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"One-to-one\">one-to-one</a> over each period of its domain. \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/8/198940adbd72848c6fa5e60346edc7a47a0f576f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19x \\equiv 141 \\pmod{180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35da5b9221fc84ae36849983d107573a8439ec80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19^2 \\equiv 361 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"19\" />, multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/96102cd3ad4d565fa6e5af1acaa2a45dc982d1c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\equiv 141 \\cdot 19 \\equiv (140+1)(18+1) \\equiv 0+140+18+1 \\equiv 159 \\pmod{180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"548\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, the smallest positive solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe29739d6588ce350ca6c9bde29229c349275ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{159}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94ef1670859133907008017a0d23e3f4def073ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\cos{96^{\\circ}}+\\sin{96^{\\circ}}}{\\cos{96^{\\circ}}-\\sin{96^{\\circ}}} = \\dfrac{1 + \\tan{96^{\\circ}}}{1-\\tan{96^{\\circ}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"243\" height=\"38\" />\nwhich is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/7/cf7060a5d07c58b1430ac62fbff257e0b5c02d37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\tan{45^{\\circ}} + \\tan{96^{\\circ}}}{1-\\tan{45^{\\circ}}\\tan{96^{\\circ}}} = \\tan{141{^\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"235\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/c/25c95ed1b2c856d539b7a3f75d98e7f660787a65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19x = 141 +180n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"14\" />, for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\nMultiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/064ae099ef8a1c67497cf49aaba54fe2712defb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\equiv 141 \\cdot 19 \\equiv 2679 \\equiv 159 \\pmod{180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"294\" height=\"18\" />.\nThe smallest positive solution of this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe29739d6588ce350ca6c9bde29229c349275ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{159}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Only_sine_and_cosine_sum_formulas.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Only_sine_and_cosine_sum_formulas)\">Solution 3 (Only sine and cosine sum formulas)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Only sine and cosine sum formulas)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It seems reasonable to assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/b/cbb8bc824f399ecd52b8d47e7adbf165963b00fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\cos{96^{\\circ}}+\\sin{96^{\\circ}}}{\\cos{96^{\\circ}}-\\sin{96^{\\circ}}} = \\tan{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"195\" height=\"40\" /> for some angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb94f91a8e01ebc5f136b04dbb7db9bc8c3b8ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{\\alpha (\\cos{96^{\\circ}}+\\sin{96^{\\circ}})}{\\alpha (\\cos{96^{\\circ}}-\\sin{96^{\\circ}})} = \\frac{\\sin{\\theta}}{\\cos{\\theta}}\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"43\" /> for some constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. We can set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/047756adc07e05f2dd4bc196e4656d3cd90d0f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha (\\cos{96^{\\circ}}+\\sin{96^{\\circ}}) = \\sin{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"213\" height=\"20\" />.Note that if we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> equal to both the sine and cosine of an angle, we can use the sine sum formula (and the cosine sum formula on the denominator). So, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74d187c449419c459f8b9a12d222a0f6cd136797.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{45^{\\circ}} = \\cos{45^{\\circ}} = \\tfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"176\" height=\"26\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8358286f90dd2702dd80cfb96c42db9f807d845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha = \\tfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"59\" height=\"26\" /> we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80c07b68188aa0f3a8d9e408fdd124185bf55f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\alpha (\\cos{96^{\\circ}} + \\sin{96^{\\circ}}) = \\cos{96^{\\circ}} \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\sin{96^{\\circ}} \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} = \\cos{96^{\\circ}} \\sin{45^{\\circ}} + \\sin{96^{\\circ}} \\cos{45^{\\circ}} = \\sin({45^{\\circ} + 96^{\\circ}}) = \\sin{141^{\\circ}}\\]\" width=\"813\" height=\"41\" />\nfrom the sine sum formula. For the denominator, from the cosine sum formula, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/0/910f7e6cb019d5385eed4c17ab6e083cfd406674.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\alpha (\\cos{96^{\\circ}} - \\sin{96^{\\circ}}) = \\cos{96^{\\circ}} \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + \\sin{96^{\\circ}} \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} = \\cos{96^{\\circ}} \\cos{45^{\\circ}} + \\sin{96^{\\circ}} \\sin{45^{\\circ}} = \\cos({96^{\\circ}  + 45^{\\circ}}) = \\cos{141^{\\circ}}.\\]\" width=\"822\" height=\"41\" />\nThis means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39763f61a26ee836d29d09c1d7c56edc553fcaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = 141^{\\circ},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74a8abc9ac23d2a251a3bb19c306ae824482ac93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19x = 141 + 180k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" /> for some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> (since the period of tangent is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />), or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/6466f25c64d61941f4c760e1288b968d560a2e91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 x \\equiv 141 \\pmod{180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" />. Note that the inverse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> is itself as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/1/701118cd3c62697754c412f77f55e598f4114d72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19^2 \\equiv 361 \\equiv 1 \\pmod {180}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"203\" height=\"21\" />, so multiplying this congruence by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> on both sides gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6df96bcdcfd7ef09e55cdf6f6d7b266f61b150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\equiv 2679 \\equiv 159 \\pmod{180}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"20\" /> For the smallest possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/3/ae3bbe725d163f94cbc07be9a4ac0aae192edf22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{159}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"80\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Multiplying the numerator and denominator of the right-hand side by\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9ccdb295aa1d9fbdb240e3dbeba184737c37647.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(96^{\\circ})+\\sin(96^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />, we get \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c82abbc9e47b535e35ee8f9985211d53c20c9c86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\tan(19x^{\\circ})}  ={\\frac{\\cos(96^{\\circ}) +\\sin(96^{\\circ})}{\\cos(96^{\\circ})-\\sin(96^{\\circ})}}\\times{\\frac{\\cos(96^{\\circ})+\\sin(96^{\\circ})}{\\cos(96^{\\circ})+\\sin(96^{\\circ})}} \\\\  ={\\frac{(\\cos(96^{\\circ})+\\sin(96^{\\circ}))^2}{\\cos^2(96^{\\circ})-\\sin^2(96^{\\circ})}} \\\\  ={\\frac{\\cos^2(96^{\\circ}) + 2\\cos(96^{\\circ})\\sin(96^{\\circ}) + \\sin^2(96^{\\circ})}{\\cos(192^{\\circ})}} \\\\  ={\\frac{1+\\sin(192^{\\circ})}{\\cos(192^{\\circ})}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"182\" />\n</p><p>Using the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1f0a0da7731f043d98c057ee81ae0c0965c5513.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta)=\\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{\\cos(\\theta)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"127\" height=\"45\" />, we get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ecc5faf65691543276b86b673790440b6ceb691.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(19x^{\\circ})=\\frac{\\sin(19x^{\\circ})}{\\cos(19x^{\\circ})}=\\frac{1+\\sin(192^{\\circ})}{\\cos(192^{\\circ})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"312\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Cross-multiplying, we find that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6be86a59c662c5efc62972d166351135f0cb6e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(19x^{\\circ})\\cos(192^{\\circ})=\\cos(19x^{\\circ})+\\cos(19x^{\\circ})\\sin(192^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"421\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Rearranging the equation gives us\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef1643f3fb7eecc120e367a6a93ccea6287463f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(19x^{\\circ})=\\sin(19x^{\\circ})\\cos(192^{\\circ})-\\cos(19x^{\\circ})\\sin(192^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"421\" height=\"20\" />\nwhich leads us to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/a/7aa1c0e765245272b17f272c36c20940ec728a27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(19x^{\\circ})=\\sin(19x-192^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"223\" height=\"20\" /> by the sine difference formula.\n</p><p>Using the identity that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83a8283fc73b1d54e8b9d879ef8ad718cf9f5c55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\theta)=\\sin(90^{\\circ}-\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" />, we find that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a31f0a9c387e65bcd707beb354957332f15a2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(90-19x^{\\circ})=\\sin(19x-192^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"261\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/7/977aa2c794d3c6270e1fd0dff5b2a323a967e95c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90-19x \\equiv 19x-192 \\pmod{360}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"264\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/1/a711b0afa306b382957872176486eff80420afcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38x \\equiv 282 \\pmod{360}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f24c4e7abcfa386ea0590a56c5a0aa44fc2cdead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38 \\times 9=342$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbde3143c0015c449fd9b8860c0a3e2562b5dd93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38 \\times 10 \\equiv 20 \\pmod{360}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"193\" height=\"20\" /> (by simple arithmetic). \nTo \"make\" <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/ead8ea40efad9858229067e6824c5cb06c5afc6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$282$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> we subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> three times from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/1/481aa8fd3205ddca64b0c5f46dab544c8a74aa36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-21$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>Finally, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/e/f8e600ed2a54da0a6495d914bad0f5eab14a1fc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360|38 \\times 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />, we can add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> to get that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a40b2cdf058f887870ea191aa88480e382893a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=180-21=\\boxed{159}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"167\" height=\"25\" /> which is the final answer.\n</p><p>~primenumbersfun\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/8/7b84194d302f2a7b740d668aa92ff5753181bb5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 45^\\circ = \\cos 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, all terms in the numerator and the denominator could be multiplied by either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d74f87367e27a00126c2b63ed0aa3d3b6d2ee947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/6828c8778bc0a8f580dc2c66ef9862c6fe7ec7d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d4b7ec30ae4dd6ab9fb6e8e74889880bad5fbda.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}     \\frac{\\cos 96^\\circ + \\sin 96^\\circ}{\\cos 96^\\circ - \\sin 96^\\circ}     &amp;= \\frac{\\cos 96^\\circ \\sin 45^\\circ + \\sin 96^\\circ \\cos 45^\\circ}{\\cos 96^\\circ \\cos 45^\\circ - \\sin 96^\\circ \\sin 45^\\circ} \\\\[0.5em]     &amp;= \\frac{\\sin(96 + 45)^\\circ}{\\cos(96 + 45)^\\circ} \\\\[0.5em]     &amp;= \\tan 141^\\circ \\end{align*}\" width=\"392\" height=\"126\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/325fffbd172955c238077dc5e15cdccfe41887b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan19x^\\circ = \\tan 141^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"156\" height=\"15\" />. In other words, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74a8abc9ac23d2a251a3bb19c306ae824482ac93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19x = 141 + 180k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9e81a562b6d5190cdc3538ea60f9a70982a4a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}     141 + 180k &amp;\\equiv 0 \\pmod{19} \\\\     8 + 9k &amp;\\equiv 0 \\pmod{19} \\\\     9k &amp;\\equiv 11 \\pmod{19} \\\\     9k &amp;\\equiv 11, 30, 49, 68, 87, 106, 125, 144 \\pmod{19} \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"428\" height=\"93\" />\nSubstituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/d/e8de1519e920807ccca3ebf36169dd580196d4de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e11bf91bdfaffb951364ffffdebfa1814aa1de1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$141 + 180 \\cdot 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/6/dd6174545a688cb70db5ab8cb7c0fac30a0f3077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{159}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~MaPhyCom\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME\" title=\"1996 AIME\">1996 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1996 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1996\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1996 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016205154\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.046 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 447/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1768/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 90/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 15945/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.682      1 -total\n 59.97%    7.605      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.32%    4.860      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wik